  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_042 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat, acc=0.7150), and scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l is clearly the strongest encoder pair (vs. pca_n2000 at 0.629 and resnet50 at 0.632). Concat fusion slightly outperforms weighted fusion (0.715 vs 0.706). The main untested dimension for improving on the current best is the aggregation method: avgpool is a simple mean, while transformer aggregation can model inter-profile interactions. This experiment (config_018: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) isolates the effect of upgrading aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other proven-optimal components fixed. It is the cleanest logical extension of the current best and directly tests whether more expressive profile aggregation can push accuracy above 0.715. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds attention computation over profiles, so I estimate ~5.5–6.5 GPU hours (moderately higher than the 4.49 h of config_042 but still well within budget). With 5 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information next step: if it improves, it opens a new promising direction; if it doesn't, it confirms avgpool is sufficient and I can pivot to other dimensions (e.g., scgpt encoder or single-profile) in later experiments."
}

